  "term": "herniation",
  "definition": "Herniation, in this context, means brain tissue being pushed out of its normal position because pressure inside the skull has become too high. It is a life-threatening condition that can disrupt consciousness and other neurological functions and is linked with poor outcomes and higher risk of death.",
